    "type": "question",
    "label": "15",
    "prompt": "Does the equation $xy=0$ represent a hyperbola? Explain your answer.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "No. The graph is the union of the $x$-axis and the $y$-axis.",
      "worked": "By the zero-product law, $xy=0$ requires $x=0$ or $y=0$. These equations describe the $y$-axis and the $x$-axis respectively, so the graph consists of the two coordinate axes rather than a hyperbola.",
